DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ddeevvffss__xxxxxx__ccddeevvpprriivv() family of functions allows the _c_d_e_v driver meth‐
     ods to associate some driver-specific data with each user process open(2)
     of the device special file.  Currently, functioning of these functions is
     restricted to the context of the _c_d_e_v_s_w switch method calls performed as
     devfs(5) operations in response to system calls that use filedescriptors.

     The ddeevvffss__sseett__ccddeevvpprriivv() function associates a data pointed by _p_r_i_v with
     current calling context (filedescriptor).  The data may be retrieved
     later, possibly from another call performed on this filedescriptor, by
     the ddeevvffss__ggeett__ccddeevvpprriivv() function.  The ddeevvffss__cclleeaarr__ccddeevvpprriivv() disassoci‐
     ates previously attached data from context.  Immediately after
     ddeevvffss__cclleeaarr__ccddeevvpprriivv() finished operating, the _d_t_r callback is called,
     with private data supplied _d_a_t_a argument.  The ddeevvffss__cclleeaarr__ccddeevvpprriivv()
     function will be also be called if the open callback function returns an
     error code.

     On the last filedescriptor close, system automatically arranges
     ddeevvffss__cclleeaarr__ccddeevvpprriivv() call.

     If successful, the functions return 0.

     The function ddeevvffss__sseett__ccddeevvpprriivv() returns the following values on error:

     [ENOENT]           The current call is not associated with some
                        filedescriptor.

     [EBUSY]            The private driver data is already associated with
                        current filedescriptor.

     The function ddeevvffss__ggeett__ccddeevvpprriivv() returns the following values on error:

     [EBADF]            The current call is not associated with some
                        filedescriptor.

     [ENOENT]           The private driver data was not associated with cur‐
                        rent filedescriptor, or ddeevvffss__cclleeaarr__ccddeevvpprriivv() was
                        called.

     The function ddeevvffss__ffoorreeaacchh__ccddeevvpprriivv() sequentially calls the function _c_b
     for each ccddeevvpprriivv structure, currently associated with the _c_d_e_v device.
     The iterated ccddeevvpprriivv data pointer and the user-supplied context _a_r_g are
     passed to the function _c_b.  If _c_b returns non-zero value, the iteration
     stops on that element.  The ddeevvffss__ffoorreeaacchh__ccddeevvpprriivv() returns the return
     value from the last call to _c_b, or zero if no ccddeevvpprriivv data is currently
     associated with the device.

     Current implementation of the iterator makes it impossible to use any
     blockable locking inside the callback _c_b.

